[executive]
# ============================================================================
# O_o_Reader validation deck: a stiffener glued edge-on to a panel (SOL 101)
#
# Validates:
#   - which grid points of a stiffener whose edge lies on the mid surface of a
#     panel the solver glues, with the panel's thickness (COPTM default: the edge is
#     inside the panel, 2 mm below its skin) and without it (COPTM1 61, format reference
#     BCTABLE remark 9: "for node-to-segment with edge-to-edge glue contact,
#     use B=6"): the punched glue equations (NLOPRM MPCPCH)
# Run notes:
#   - bring the .pch back with the listing and the result data
# Written for this project, to exercise the reader.
# How to run it, what to bring back: validation/models/README.md.
# ============================================================================
SolutionSequence;101
[case]
TitleText;O_o_Reader validation: a stiffener glued edge-on to a panel
BulkEcho;Sorted
NonlinearOutputParams;PunchGlueEquations
ContactSelection;1
SinglePointConstrSelection;1
StaticLoadSelection;1
DisplacementOutput;All;PlotOnly
MultiPointConstrForceOutput;All;PlotOnly
SubcaseStart;1
LabelText;loads on the stiffeners
[model]
Parameter;PostprocessingFile;-1
ResultFileParams;Precision;64;CompressionMethod;GzipCompression
# Two assemblies 100 mm apart, each a 40 x 40 panel of 2 x 2 CQUAD4 at z = 0,
# 4 mm thick (PSHELL 1), and a stiffener of 2 CQUAD4 in the plane y = 15, x 5
# to 35, z 0 to 30, 2 mm thick (PSHELL 2), whose lower edge lies on the mid
# surface of the panel. Assembly A (bodies 1, 2) leaves the panel's thickness
# out (COPTM1 61), assembly B (bodies 3, 4) keeps the defaults. Units: mm, N,
# tonne.
IsoMat;1;7.E+4;;0.33;2.7E-9
ShellProp;1;1;4.;1;;1
ShellProp;2;1;2.;1;;1
Node;1;;0.;0.;0.
Node;2;;20.;0.;0.
